>So my question is:  what special powers does the Tsurugi have? (beyond
>cutting beasties in half, that is).  Should I dump my blessed rustproof
>Excalibur and blessed +3 silver saber in favor of this artifact weapon?
>And, why is GDSM so highly lauded? Is it automatically rustproof?  (if
>so I wasted grease on it).

You probably Don't want to dump them.  Many artifacts are particularly
useful in certain situations.  Excalibur will give you an added defense
at the appropriate time;  it is possible that your silver may even do
a larger amount of damage than the tsurugi to the appropriate monsters.

Also, as someone indicated, you can't use a shield while wielding the
Tsurugi.  You may find a time when you want to use a shield, so you'll
want to have a good weapon for that circumstance.  I also don't know
off hand whether the Tsurugi is initially rustproff -- if it isn't
you'll want a different weapon for Those circumstances as well.
(both monsters and traps can provide rust).

>
>[I have come to appreciate the regular silver saber -- sears flesh of
>lycanthropes, demons, and I think it sears some undead too.  And it doesn't
>rust.  When my SnickerSnee rusted to death and I couldn't get anything good
>by sacrificing, my silver saber was an adequate weapon.  So I'm loathe to
>chuck it unless the Tsurugi is such a super weapon I'll never whip out my
>saber again.]

I'd recommend holding on to it.  At least until you know the Tsurugi
is rustproofed -- and until you know you are sure you won't be needing
a shield any more.  I won't spell out this latter comment, since any
spoiler about wonderful shields is relatively irrelevant here.

